problem:
Problem description
- There are $$I$$ customer orders indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$.
- Each order $$i$$ is characterized by a required width $$w_i$$ and a required length $$\ell_i$$.
- There are $$S$$ available standard stock width types indexed by $$s \in \mathcal{S}$$, with standard width parameter $$W_s$$ for each type.
- The stock length is effectively unlimited, and length pieces may be spliced together, so the main planning decision is how to cut widths and allocate material area.
- The planning goal is to choose a cutting plan that satisfies all orders while minimizing total waste area.
- Business rules:
  - Only stock widths in $$\mathcal{S}$$ may be used.
  - Every order must be fully satisfied in both width and length.
  - Length fulfillment may come from multiple spliced pieces when needed.
  - Any unused material area created by cutting is counted as waste.
  - The solution should minimize the total waste area across all used stock material.
- A solution is represented by:
  - A set of cutting patterns $$\mathcal{P}$$.
  - A pattern usage variable $$x_p$$ for each $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, indicating how many times pattern $$p$$ is applied.
  - A pattern composition description for each $$p$$, identifying the stock width type used and the orders included in that pattern.
  - A total waste area value $$Z$$.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "meaning": "static single planning horizon; no time indexing is required"
  },
  "orders": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "$$I$$",
    "items": {
      "order_id": "identifier in $$\\mathcal{I}$$",
      "required_width": "real demand parameter $$w_i \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$",
      "required_length": "real demand parameter $$\\ell_i \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$"
    }
  },
  "stock_widths": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "$$S$$",
    "items": {
      "stock_width_id": "identifier in $$\\mathcal{S}$$",
      "standard_width": "real parameter $$W_s \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$"
    }
  },
  "splicing_allowed": "boolean parameter indicating whether length pieces may be joined",
  "objective": "minimize total waste area"
}

Output Format
{
  "selected_patterns": {
    "type": "array",
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "items": {
      "pattern_id": "identifier in $$\\mathcal{P}$$",
      "stock_width_id": "identifier in $$\\mathcal{S}$$",
      "usage_count": "nonnegative integer $$x_p \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\ge 0}$$",
      "orders_in_pattern": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "order_id": "identifier in $$\\mathcal{I}$$",
          "allocated_width": "width assigned to the order in this pattern, consistent with $$w_i$$",
          "allocated_length": "length assigned to the order in this pattern, consistent with $$\\ell_i$$"
        }
      },
      "pattern_waste_area": "nonnegative real value $$Z_p \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$"
    }
  },
  "total_waste_area": "nonnegative real value $$Z \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$$"
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": "single static period",
  "orders": [
    {
      "order_id": 1,
      "required_width": 0.5,
      "required_length": 1000
    },
    {
      "order_id": 2,
      "required_width": 0.7,
      "required_length": 3000
    },
    {
      "order_id": 3,
      "required_width": 0.9,
      "required_length": 2000
    }
  ],
  "stock_widths": [
    {
      "stock_width_id": 1,
      "standard_width": 1
    },
    {
      "stock_width_id": 2,
      "standard_width": 2
    }
  ],
  "splicing_allowed": true
}
